# Cloudflare — required for the web runtime (Pages Functions) to read
# the catalog produced by the data pipeline AND to deploy new
# releases to https://token-factory-initializr.pages.dev. Copy this
# file to ``.env`` and fill in the values, or set the same variables
# in your shell.
#
# Without these:
#   * ``wrangler pages dev`` runs but ``/api/*`` returns 404 (KV empty).
#   * ``wrangler pages deploy`` fails with an auth error.
#
# Get the values from:
#   * account id    — Cloudflare dashboard → right sidebar
#   * web token     — dash.cloudflare.com → "My Profile" → "API Tokens"
#                     (template "Edit Cloudflare Pages" gives Pages edit
#                     + Workers KV read; that's all the web needs).
#                     This is the **read-only-from-KV + Pages-deploy**
#                     token. The data pipeline uses a separate token
#                     with KV write permission (see data/.env).
#   * namespace     — ``wrangler kv namespace list`` (the existing
#                     ``magi-kv`` namespace is what the data pipeline
#                     writes to; the web reads from it).
#
# Token-split rationale: scoping each token to the minimum required
# permissions means a leak of the web token can't be used to overwrite
# the catalog, and a leak of the data token can't be used to deploy
# arbitrary code to Pages. Both tokens share the same account id and
# namespace id by design.
CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID=
CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=
CLOUDFLARE_KV_NAMESPACE_ID=0d4734eae9ce4b5d9ad4fa32e6ef462c

# When set to "1", Pages Functions skip KV lookups and serve the bundled
# fixture file (web/functions/lib/fixtures.ts). Useful when KV is empty
# (e.g. fresh clone before the data pipeline has run). Defaults to "0"
# so production deployments always hit the live KV.
#
# Local dev: pass ``--var TFI_USE_LOCAL_FIXTURES=1`` on the wrangler CLI,
# or use ``npm run dev`` which sets it for you.
TFI_USE_LOCAL_FIXTURES=0